                        "review": "Disclaimer: At the time of writing this review, I haven't completly finished the game.\n\nJump, Step, Step is an entertaining game with cute graphics. But don't let the first impression fool you, this game gets really challenging after the first few stages.\n\nThe concept is similar to games such as Lightbot. You control a little robot (called Bob) stranded in a world full of dangerous cliffs, spikes and breaking stones. You'll have to program Bob by clicking together a chain of commands. Bob will faithfully execute your defined commands. If he doesn't reach the goal, you'll lose a life (in form of a battery). If you have no lives left, you'll have to start over at a checkpoint.\n\nAs you progress in the game, the stages will become harder and you'll gradually unlock more complex commands. You'll have to think of clever ways to help Bob reach the goal. In the later levels, you'll inevitable fail a few times before you get the right idea and you have to start over at a checkpoint.\n\nUnfortunately, there's no ingame indication when you have reached a checkpoint and sometimes the placement of the checkpoints is annoying because they're too far away from where you failed. The translation of the dialogues is okay, tough not perfect (I accidentally lost an early save because of a misleading german translation of the menu option \"clear saved game\").\n\nDespite of it's minor shortcomings, the game is definitly worth the price and the right choice for everybody who likes to program and/or puzzle! Even experienced programmers will get their money's worth with this game!",
